+## 5h. Wave 8, as built (the treatment's playable aftermath, in the epilogue)
+
+**Status (13.11): Automated runtime only.** Built and verified by the bot and the suites on SwiftShader; nobody has played it,
+nothing was listened to (the valve, the running water and the shut are the game's existing synthesized sounds), no frame rate
+measured. The first worker on this wave was lost with its session (its commit and its uncommitted test edits survived in the
+worktree); the wave was finished, verified and written up in a second session.
+
+**Wave 8's verification** (port 8920 snapshot of this branch, the base `516f6145` on 8921; one suite at a time):
+
+SUITE_TABLE
+
+| Chapter | Before (base) | Now: what the player does | Where |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Epilogue | the dinner (seven lines at the table), then at once the end screen; Keep Exploring. The kitchen tap of chapter 1 was never turned again. A save made at the epilogue's start (before the dinner) loaded into a quiet house with "Go home. Dinner is waiting" and no end screen ever came | The dinner as it was, at the table (he sits down for it, not in the hall's doorway). Then "Later. Empty plates, and most of the story told." Arthur: "Dad! Come and turn the tap. I want to hear the pipe." Zoé: "He's had his ear on that pipe for four days. Go on." **Control in the kitchen**: Arthur by the dresser beside the sink, listening; Zoé by the table, drying her hands; Arthur's cup under the spout, empty. The objective: "Turn the kitchen tap. Arthur is listening". The door holds ("Arthur is waiting by the tap."); Zoé: "The tap first. He won't let anyone else near it." **The tap**: his hand on the cross's knob turns it (the handle turns under it), the water runs cold into the cup and fills it, and the wall stays quiet (no knock is played). The first time, a short close look from over the stove, along the wall, at the spout, the stream and the cup (off under `?nocine`). "(Cold. And not one knock in the wall.)" Arthur: "Nothing! Not three, not four. It just runs." "My cup stays under it, though. Just in case." "In case of what?" "In case it stops. Then I'll know first." He shuts it again (his hand on the knob once more); the cup stays full under the spout. **Zoé's word**: "Bram came by. The lane runs cold too. Hedda is washing everything she owns." "Then it's done." "Nearly. You told us everything, slowly. Except the guardian. You went very fast over the guardian." "It was a very fast guardian." "Sit down. Start there." → the end screen. After Keep Exploring the tap is still a tap: "(Cold. Still quiet.)" | `story/hometap.js` (`EpilogueTap`), `story/epilogue.js`, `interiors.js` (the tap's handle), `text/thread.js` |
+
+**Why this shape.** The campaign opened on a dry tap that knocked: the player turned it by hand, carried Arthur's cup from the
+wrong pipe to the right one, and followed the knock out of the house (wave 1); Arthur counted it in chapter 10 and heard the
+signal in chapter 12. The ending pays that off in the same room, with the same hand action and the same cup, and the change is
+unmistakable without a speech: the water is cold and the wall is quiet. Arthur's "just in case" keeps him the boy who listens to
+the pipe, not a hero; Zoé's word closes the lane she saved in chapter 8 (Bram, Hedda) and sends the player back to the table,
+warm and ordinary. Short: three lines to set it up, five at the tap, five with Zoé. No new region, no new person, no new voice,
+no night words (the dinner's lines had none either).
+
+**New flags only** (old saves load and go on): `ep_v ep_tap ep_word`. `ep_v` is set when the epilogue begins, or on loading
+an epilogue save from before whose dinner is still ahead (`base-16`): such a save now plays the dinner (it loaded into a quiet
+house before, with no end screen) and the kitchen's step after it. A save from before past the dinner (`base-16-end`,
+`base-16-free`) has no `ep_v`: the step counts as done, the door is open, the objective is "See how everyone is doing", and the
+tap is there to turn (cold, quiet); the cup stands under it. Saved: after the setup lines (the kitchen's step), after the tap,
+after Zoé's word.
+
+**Hands.** One new hand action, through `story/reach.js` (`touchWater` at the cross's height): his hand on the knob toward the
+room, to turn the tap open and again to shut it. The handle stood 0.73 m over the sink's back, out of his reach from the
+cupboard's front; it is now on a short stem at the end of the pipe's run (5.5 cm lower, 6 cm nearer the room); the spout has
+not moved. The opening film's tap (Zoé's hand, `opening.js`) reads the handle's position, so it follows. Measured in
+`tests/campaign-hands.mjs`: 0.2 cm opened, 0.2 cm shut. Zoé's apron wipe is her own body's surface (listed, as `no-air.mjs`).
+
